Abstract: The FAIR Data Train Visit Protocol specifies the conversation between a Train Handler and a Data Station for one <em>visit</em> — one train, at one station, under one agreement. It covers how a visit is dispatched (by push, or by a station that accepts no inbound connection polling for it), how the station checks what arrived, how an agreement is negotiated on arrival and signed by both parties before anything runs, how every decision the station takes is reported as an event with a justification, how a result is inspected before it leaves and how state is handed from one visit to the next by location and digest and never by value. It defines the three message types — the visit descriptor, the visit event and the visit-result envelope — the two HTTP interfaces, the outcome vocabulary a completeness statement reports to a data consumer verbatim, and what a conforming station and a conforming Handler must do.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no, idl no, dfn yes, biblio yes
