  <tr><td>Handler API, station-facing<td>OpenAPI 3.1, `1.1.0-draft.1`<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/protocol/openapi/handler-callback-api.yaml">`protocol/openapi/handler-callback-api.yaml`</a>
  <tr><td>ODRL profile and shapes<td>`https://w3id.org/fdt/profile`<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/vocab/fdt-profile.ttl">`vocab/fdt-profile.ttl`</a>, <a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/shapes/policy.shapes.ttl">`shapes/policy.shapes.ttl`</a> (`fdts:RequestShape`, `fdts:AgreementShape`, `fdts:SignatureShape`)
  <tr><td>Run vocabulary<td>`https://w3id.org/fdt/run#`<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/vocab/fdt-run.ttl">`vocab/fdt-run.ttl`</a>
  <tr><td>Agreement derivation (rule and checker)<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/protocol/agreement-derivation.md">`protocol/agreement-derivation.md`</a>, `tools/derivation.py`
  <tr><td>Result inspection (rule and checker)<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/protocol/result-inspection.md">`protocol/result-inspection.md`</a>, `tools/inspection.py`
  <tr><td>Dispatch credential<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/protocol/dispatch-credential.md">`protocol/dispatch-credential.md`</a>
  <tr><td>Canonical form<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/tools/canonical.py">`tools/canonical.py`</a>, cross-checked against the RDF Dataset Canonicalization reference implementation
  <tr><td>DSP mapping<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/blob/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/mapping/state-machines.md">`mapping/state-machines.md`</a>
  <tr><td>Fixtures<td>—<td><a href="https://github.com/FAIRDataTeam/fdt-commons/tree/eaa339c1c6749997bf93fe00bf9cc967291ce3cb/examples/protocol">`examples/protocol/`</a>
</table>

The `https://w3id.org/fdt/…` identifiers are the names these artefacts carry in the contracts.
Their redirects are not yet published; until they are, the locations above are where the artefacts
resolve.

<h2 class="no-num" id="changes">Appendix C: Change history</h2>

*This appendix is non-normative.*

: 16 October 2026 — no station types
:: The protocol never had a station type for identifier translation, but it spoke of "a linkage
    station" as though it did. It now says what it meant: an ordinary station hosting a translation
    service, named in the descriptor's `linkageStation` ([[#outbound]]). The member names `linkage`
    and `linkageStation` are contract names and are unchanged.
: 16 October 2026 — conformance criteria
:: [[#conformance]] gains the numbered criteria of [[#criteria]] — STA for every station, PUSH
    and POLL for the two dispatch classes, HND for the Handler — each naming the section that
    states it and the fixture, checker or harness that checks it; the optional features; and the
    form of a conformance statement. `GET /agreements/{agreementId}` is now listed among the
    operations a push-dispatch station implements, which the signature exchange already required.
    No normative requirement changed; one indicative sentence ([[#parties]], the self-description
    advertisement) now carries the key word it was always read with.
: 16 October 2026 — version 1, editors' draft
:: First publication as a specification, written against `fdt-commons` 0.75.0 and the running
    reference implementation. Relative to the draft-1 protocol note of 12 September 2026 inside
    `fdt-commons`: both parties sign the agreement (ADR-038) and the exchange has a poll-dispatch
    shape (Q52); the dispatch credential is graded (ADR-044); a station may read the redacted plan
    (ADR-047); hand-over has an inbound direction, named by location and digest (Q124), with the
    lineage rule and `https`-only locations; the agreement lifecycle has an `awaiting signature`
    state; and the derivation rule binds the agreement's parties to the offer's and the request's.
